CAMEL role-playing adaptation for Slick

This folder adapts algorithm logic and prompt templates from:
CAMEL-AI, https://github.com/camel-ai/camel
Release v0.1.0, commit bda4bf43bb03092936c2c0316aee9ff96aa551bf
Licensed under Apache License 2.0; see LICENSE.

The task, assistant, user, and critic prompt wording was adapted from
camel/prompts/ai_society.py. Role-playing and proposal-selection behavior was
adapted from camel/agents/role_playing.py and camel/agents/critic_agent.py.
Changes include Slick decorators, external Jinja templates, explicit transcript
rendering, caller-supplied providers, typed critic selection, protocol guards,
and explicit failure records. The solution extraction prompt is from Appendix H
of the user-supplied CAMEL paper.

Paper: Guohao Li, Hasan Abed Al Kader Hammoud, Hani Itani, Dmitrii Khizbullin,
and Bernard Ghanem. CAMEL: Communicative Agents for “Mind” Exploration of Large
Language Model Society (2023).
